Package: fluxqc
Type: Package
Title: Detection Limits, Quality Screens and Ebullition for Chamber Flux
    Measurements, on Top of 'goFlux'
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Gewirtzman", email = "jongewirtzman@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Works on any closure processed with the 'goFlux' package
    (Rheault et al. 2024, <doi:10.21105/joss.06393>), whatever the surface:
    soil, water, tree stems, branches, leaves or any other chamber
    enclosure, diffusive or ebullitive. Adds empirical precision and minimum
    detectable flux by several published methods with detection flags,
    toggleable physical quality screens that only append columns, an opt-in
    ebullition (bubble) add-on, multi-gas window selection, non-interactive
    window detection, a one-call pipeline with explicit outputs, a PDF
    exporter compatible with 'ggplot2' >= 3.5, import helpers for very large
    LI-7810 files and clock utilities. All functions keep 'goFlux' column
    conventions and never modify a 'goFlux' column. The bundled examples come
    from the author's tree-stem, soil and open-water campaigns; tree stems
    are one application, not the scope.
